  ('zcrm_1579374000031937003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000031936015', 'Brian Schey', NULL, '3-4-19 Wanted HEP but he learned 2 years ago that he has a smaller coronary artery than most and was born with it. It won''t affect his life but he is asked to have it checked 1x per year. He recognizes it''s not worth the risk in case something happens. Could put a stint in but isn''t doing so now. Did what sounds like nuclear stress test. Missed open enrollment so can''t join HEP. Therefore, STM is the only choice. We kept the Cancer/Stroke/Heart attack $25K Indemnity plan, plus, Accident Plan with National General for $224.92 a month. He''s enrolling now and chose the 2 6 month term options to try to get him through to open enrollment for 2020. Lost both parents in previous 5 months! Income is $35K but will get inheritances with ongoing investment income.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-03-04 16:11:12', '2019-03-04 16:11:12'),
