  ('zcrm_1579374000030801003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005030392', 'Deborah Badgley', NULL, 'Member left VM requesting to update her pmt information.  I sent out link.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-02-11 07:14:13', '2019-02-11 07:14:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000030735058', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032601016', 'Meggan Kramer', NULL, '2-8-19 Employment is changing soon so she''ll be an Ind. Contractor and losing ins. either March 1st or April 1st. She has asthma and never been to hospital for it fortunately. She has a preventative inhaler and a fast acting inhaler. She''s now paying $208 a month through Kaiser now that they are supposedly covering part of it since it cost $600. But, before that it was costing her only $45. Through World Med RX Dulera 100/5 x 3inhalers 385.58 + 9.95, therefore about $133 a month! She also takes anxiety meds and those are affordable so she''s not worried about those. She will absorb everything and we will revisit next Friday.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-02-08 16:10:42', '2019-02-08 16:10:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000030724033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000026675058', 'Anthony Peck', NULL, 'Anthony wanted to know where to send preventative care bills to so I gave him the email address, he also wanted to know why the cards didn''t have his wifes name, I explained that as well, he also wanted to know how to present himself at hospitals and dr offices- I explained and sent him the script.- KC', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-02-08 14:43:21', '2019-02-08 14:43:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000030724028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005116123', 'Ronald Levis', NULL, 'Ronald called in just sounding awful, he said that he went to Africa for a few weeks and now has horrible chills and is shaking.  He went to the doctor yesterday and they could not find anything besides something wrong with his kidney values, he mentioned having a malaria test and they told him to hold off because it is a very expensive $3,000 test.  He is going back to see the doctor on tuesday- if he is the same or worse he is going to ask the doctor again for the test.  I kinda did a crash course welcome call because he hadn''t had one, and now that he is sick he needed to know quite a bit.  I recommended that if his health declines and he had questions about any testing that would go over the $1,000 IUA to give Sedera a call and they would walk him through that process.  I spent a very long time on the phone with him and he said that I was very helpful but that he really needs to take notes on the welcome call!  I gave him Sedera''s phone number,  a welcome call scheduler, information on 2nd MD (if he wanted to reach out to them I STRESSED possibly) about the Malaria test, a prescription medication quote form, and how to submit bills to Sedera.  I am also going to reach out to Sedera with this info.- KC', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-02-08 14:32:01', '2019-02-08 14:32:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000030747003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005653245', 'Michel Abboud', NULL, 'member called and updated payment info. February payment processed 2/8/19', 'Vladislava Terziyska', 'Vladislava Terziyska', '2019-02-08 13:46:47', '2019-02-08 13:46:47'),
