  ('zcrm_1579374000030707006', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000004893069', 'Jane Brown', NULL, 'Hi Steve,

I am confused then.  If she was aware that our product was separated from Liberty, why did she not contact us to cancel? We have a very easy cancellation process with a form.  At some point she needs to assume consumer responsibility.  We continue to support the members we have that are still with Liberty Healthshare.  We have added services and have happy members.  The terms and conditions are on our website and the phone number comes on all the cc bills.  She refuses to submit written cancellation.  I have cancelled her without it.  This still does not explain why she called a few days ago to update her payment information.  

For the record there was never a legal battle with Liberty.  Liberty decided to take all of their sales inside that was the reason for the split.  They sent a letter to their membership regarding this.  At that point we did have members cancel.  Again member responsibility.  Her February payment was declined.  Regardless of what she claims, she does know who we are and what our services are.  We have tracking to show us that she is opening the emails.  


Kind regards,

