  ('zcrm_1579374000027271084', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005806109', 'Signe Petersen', NULL, '---- On Tue, 27 Nov 2018 17:25:30 -0500 Jane Kassel <jane@kasselbenefits.com> wrote ----

Hello Team,

I got a call from this client yesterday, and I asked her to put her request in an email.  See Below.

First of all, her HES membership needs to be cancelled immediately!
Next, she is looking for a refund, as she was not even aware she was being charged for this after she cancelled Liberty. 
What happened with her and a lot of other clients, is that she contacted Liberty directly, as she was accustomed to dealing with the carrier directly when she had traditional insurance.
She never contacted me to cancel. She did not realize/remember that there was a second part (and charge) to the HES program.  
NOTE: I explained this to every member as I sold the program, because I followed a script, but as all of you know, with the extent of info.and learning curve, this is not a part that stuck with them.

In addition, like many of us, her bills are all set up on autopay. 
...Her life was very hectic, caring for a parent that ended up passing away, then she moved out of the area, sold a house, bought another house, etc. all while turning 65 and going onto Medicare.
It was only when she went to do her taxes recently for 2017 and went through all of her statements that she saw this charge appearing monthly, not knowing what it was for. 
Investigating it, she discovered it was the Mpowering membership.

It''s a lot of money-- 
She''s very upset to have paid for something she didn''t use. She wants a full refund.

Please contact me to work out a resolution. 
Thank you,

Jane



