  ('zcrm_1579374000026735040', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012535018', 'Rodney Brandenburg', NULL, '11-13-18 Called to understand again how to handle his hernia. He gave provider his MEC card and they told him it''s not covered of course. I told him again must be self - pay. He got quote from Longmont United Hospital for hernia surgery and it was going to cost $44K! He found hospital in Parker and can have surgery with the highest up guy. Cost is $481 for 2 hrs for the dr., $1300 for the anesthesia and unsure cost of hospital. On 11-14-18 he spoke with LaShonda who told him it wouldn''t be shared because he didn''t get pre-approval. She was not nice to him and he got very upset! He later spoke with Dania who reassured him the cost will be shared above his chosen IUA and she was thrilled at the costs he''d found. She sent him an email confirming Sedera''s commitment to the cost and he was feeling much better. But, he never wants to be treated that way again by LaShonda.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-11-15 16:09:36', '2018-11-15 16:09:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000026735035', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000096791017', 'Peter Lehmann', NULL, '11-13-18 Lives in WA and runs own DPC but looking at PSDHC for his family. He''s cash paying everything already. They are currently with LHS and want to switch asap. Peter isn''t on LHS bc he has Muscular Dystrophy and was rejected. Wife had blood clot 4 years ago. He''s happy that Sedera has some mental health benefits as well. He''s not religious so feels better about Sedera. He may want to offer this to his patients as well!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-11-15 16:04:15', '2018-11-15 16:04:15'),
