  ('zcrm_1579374000026324003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027283187', 'Joan Wood', NULL, '11-7-18 She''s been self-employed for 6 mo now and husband is self-employed. She''s a graphic designer/creative director. Paying $1200 for Cigna with $7500 ded. She''s 55 and he''s 50. Both healthy, but she had hypothyroid. Thyroid was taken out many years ago and now just takes meds to manage it. She had learned of the faith based healthsharing but didn''t feel good about it bc she''s not religious. She walks and does yoga, he snowboards, wake boards, swims, etc. Told her they could fund HSA for 2018 if joins Dec. 1st.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2018-11-07 09:31:59', '2018-11-07 09:31:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000026299028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011910021', 'Sonja Ferdows', NULL, 'Sonja called needing some reassurance about being a self-pay patient.  She wanted to know if there was a program she could utilize if her foot pain, ended up being too much of a financial burden, so I told her about the 2nd MD program, and that she could use them at any time for an opinion.   Also I am going to send her a healthgrades.com search on the podiatrist she was referred to. - KC', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2018-11-07 09:16:40', '2018-11-07 09:16:40'),
